{"authored" [{"question" "q-103354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,y=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,y & =0 \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,y & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})y & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)y & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{{(-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and $Q(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/