{"question" "q-103354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to write $(\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2y+{x}^{2}}{y}$ in the standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y+{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(\\frac{2y+{x}^{2}}{y}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is in standard form with  $P(x)=-2$ and $Q(x)={x}^{2}.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1546f0e9b1bf06bff40e7bfc86b9a5dacb385ae508daadb1ff3ece564edf5238" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-y"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26