egin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x=y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x{y}^{-1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation cannot be written in standard form since the power of $y$ in the term $x{y}^{-1}$ is not $1.$ Since the equation cannot be written in standard form, we conclude that it is not a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations can be written in the standard form, and therefore they are first-order linear ODEs." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb4d28ad52ee2323cc5eba3288092cabe973f18909117f96787114c62ba4296e" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-8352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is **NOT** a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080399/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a36807b6587d2cdea76e3dff56545f2fdeb906fc8225120f941523f44e81c16"} {"question" "q-8352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to write $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x=y$ in the standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x=y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x{y}^{-1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation cannot be written in standard form since the power of $y$ in the term $x{y}^{-1}$ is not $1.$ Since the equation cannot be written in standard form, we conclude that it is not a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations can be written in the standard form, and therefore they are first-order linear ODEs." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080399/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a36807b6587d2cdea76e3dff56545f2fdeb906fc8225120f941523f44e81c16"} {"question" "q-8352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080399/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "17d5ed82e071b24b9b8925d8254b79244802620613702a0706b3182b3cda5921"} {"question" "q-8352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080399/state.json" "file_sha256" "6a36807b6587d2cdea76e3dff56545f2fdeb906